    mission: { situation: 'You are Emi. Your tutor is Akari. She is worried about identification and describes pressure to contribute beyond her capacity. She has already spoken with her parents several times and wants this conversation kept private.', task: 'Acknowledge the concern, check what she wants from the exchange and confirm that listening does not require publication.', roles: ['Akari', 'Emi'], lines: ['Emi, can I talk without this becoming something my family hears on the podcast?', 'What do you need to understand about the contributions they expect?', 'I have already explained my limits several times. How would you respond to that?', 'Does loving my family mean you assume I can afford every request?', 'Can we leave any public use undecided while you listen?'], evidence: 'Monday follow-up to Chapter 1 email, then several exchanges before private conversation. Akari is the name used in the outline; real name is not supplied or disclosed. Parents in financial difficulty and asking more, but no amount, loan, business detail or redevelopment known yet. Multiple prior family discussions. She says not yet to publication and wants listening only. No public permission, recording permission, identity guarantee or family resolution inferred.', useful: ['We can keep this conversation ...', 'What would you like from ...?', 'You have already ..., so ...', 'I would not assume that ...', 'Being heard does not mean ...'] },
