    choose: [['Jun faces a power (imbalance / imbalanced).', 'imbalance'], ['He fears (retaliation / retaliated).', 'retaliation'], ['He wants to understand the available (options / optional).', 'options'], ['He declines a recorded (interview / interviewing).', 'interview'], ['Information can help before he (decides / decide) what to do.', 'decides'], ['His interest does not (authorise / authorises) recording.', 'authorise']],
    choices: [['What has Jun chosen so far?', 'Receive information and decline a recorded interview.', 'File a formal complaint during the conversation.', 'A'], ['What is a risk he describes?', 'A confirmed dismissal already completed.', 'Possible job loss with family income at stake.', 'B'], ['Which response respects the situation?', 'Explain available channels without deciding for him.', 'Insist that declining recording proves disloyalty.', 'A'], ['What remains unconfirmed?', 'That he describes repeated humiliation.', 'A complaint, investigation or guaranteed protection from retaliation.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: 'You are Emi. Your tutor is Riku. Read the new participation review note. Explain how the team can offer information without turning Jun’s private exchange into content.', task: 'Describe the reporting barrier, distinguish the permissions and propose a response that leaves the next decision with Jun.', roles: ['Riku', 'Emi'], title: 'Jun conversation: participation review', text: '<p><strong>Next step: information without a recording condition</strong></p><p>Jun wants to understand reporting and support options before choosing a course of action. Offer the information he requested without making a recorded interview the price of receiving it.</p><p>Keep his economic concern visible in any internal discussion: his family relies on the income he fears losing. That explains a barrier without proving what an employer would do in response.</p><p>Do not describe the exchange as a recorded interview, public testimony or a submitted complaint. Jun declined recording. No employer identity, investigation outcome or guaranteed protection has been supplied. A respectful follow-up asks what information would be useful and leaves him space to decide.</p>', lines: ['Emi, what makes the reporting decision difficult in Jun’s account?', 'What information has he asked us to help him understand?', 'Can we treat his agreement to receive information as permission to record?', 'Why should recording never become a condition of our offer here?', 'What outcome should we avoid promising?', 'How could we check what he needs without choosing the next action for him?'], evidence: 'Fresh internal note, not transcript of a recorded interview. Jun reports humiliation and career threats, fears retaliation, family depends income. No named employer, recorded contribution, filed complaint, legal finding, dismissal, hotline details or guaranteed protection. Do not give employment-law advice or claim a specific procedure is current; task is respectful communication about options. Hana’s qualifications are unspecified.', useful: ['The barrier he describes is ...', 'He wants information before ...', 'That choice does not extend to ...', 'We should avoid promising ...', 'A respectful follow-up could ask ...'] },
