    mission: { situation: 'You are Riku. Your tutor is Daisuke. The café faces rising costs, weak business and unpaid bills. He has agreed to review resources but wants the disclosure kept between you. You noticed an envelope from a property management company without reading its contents.', task: 'Recognise the concern, keep the offer realistic and distinguish what you know from what the envelope makes you wonder.', roles: ['Daisuke', 'Riku'], lines: ['Riku, why does asking for help feel so difficult after twenty years?', 'Can you understand that feeling without calling the business a personal failure?', 'What exactly have you offered to help me do?', 'Does looking at resources mean you can guarantee financial support?', 'Will you keep this private for now?', 'What could you know from the outside of an envelope alone?'], evidence: 'Daisuke initial concealment, later disclosure to Riku, rising operating costs and poor business. Twenty years operating café; no debt amount, rent arrears, loan approval, insolvency finding, exact turnover, closure date or advice to borrow. Agrees to review resources, not funding already received. Privacy request stands. Property company envelope is a clue without contents; landlord redevelopment letter is only confirmed in final episode.', useful: ['It makes sense that this feels ...', 'That feeling does not prove ...', 'I can help review ...', 'We cannot assume ...', 'I will keep ... private.'] },
    topics: [['FINANCIAL SHAME', ['How can someone recognise embarrassment without reinforcing a judgement?', 'Why distinguish a difficult situation from a person’s worth?', 'What might make an offer of information easier to accept?']], ['LIMITED OFFERS', ['Why be precise about what support you can provide?', 'How does exploring resources differ from a guaranteed outcome?', 'What should remain undecided until more information is available?']], ['PRIVATE INFORMATION', ['What can an unopened envelope establish?', 'Why avoid guessing the full problem from a clue?', 'How can a supporter respect a request for privacy?']]],
    trivia: '“Keep a confidence” means respect information entrusted to you privately. Here, Daisuke agrees to review resources while asking Riku to keep the disclosure between them. Those choices concern support, not public reporting.', triviaQuestion: ['Does agreeing to private support authorise a podcast story?', 'No. Daisuke has specifically asked for privacy.'],
